<description>&lt;p&gt;Rescue operations continue after an earthquake left more than 224 dead, while protests over the removal of artworks from the National Museum have led to water-cannon use on demonstrators in Bogotá. The president is preparing to sign a decree defining maritime boundaries for the San Andres, Providencia and Santa Catalina Archipelago, and former rebel leaders have been charged with war crimes against Indigenous groups. An evangelist pastor was murdered by gang members he had evangelized, a Colombian chef was killed in a crash in Attard, and a priest died when a cross fell during a livestreamed mass. ICE agents tackled a Colombian asylum seeker in Washington, and the Mobile Anti-Riot Squad (ESMAD) has returned to operate in the country. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ABC7 Bay Area&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizgFBVV95cUxOTFM3eEhsNDBaYTlYWFZNNnRtN1RrVjVNWE1PUEVnOHE4RXhTZXJrb096Mk03NUduNkQ2N0llVGU2czJXWEtpc0pTLVI5azZKLUpiX3lUM05YNXlqNVlRbE5rVU1WVW9WY0NCZjRXdEdYcDFqUm44d3BXRUM5Y0Q1SkU1UzluM3d0UXdPeExlaEJvWGdZUmtFU25SMXdFaDhQSXB1VzBwMklDM2pBa1ZaUDZpVHlzOWk1YmpaYTZ1OFI2UE83OVBxREFMNWZXUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Justice For Colombia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxQWFdrclVzWHJ2dmlqTDVDekIxU0VhdWtMSVlXSUpwU0lYVnNmVnlObi1PenNvUTFJTVpSWnhYT1k2N21Rd2x1Uk1DMzV1eExXUFAyODIwd0VmLWZRU25INVZ6T0Y4czFFTGNIT2NnODNWSDktV3FPTDFocWxINWtiVjZYaDd3RnlBV2l2TVExMWtjeEhyQmNjdnVWVDRPRW9C?oc=5&quot;&gt;Christian Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxOS29LTmY0dUdoZkUtNExpR2d3aWVIRWU2VXVPdmhmeFdXSjBHM1VxajNDYWpzMmg3dmpPMHRRLS1Cc0c0eVhrc2ZpRmxXSWdGdjlRVlF3dkZ1N1JjcTZHYmt4MWRpOWFIMEliRGtHTW9qVzZ6ODZoQ21MMVhvUGNsMTNuWm56ZVFU